-- title:
--   Contraction commutes with powers of the Drinfeld chart centre
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q\ge 5$, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell\ge 3$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$.
--
--   **Base field and function field.** $L$ is a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity (`hξ`); `hι` requires the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((T))$ (Laurent series over $L$) which by `hK` equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield of $L((T))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, where $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, that is, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   **Coefficient ring and chart algebra.** $A$ is a discrete valuation domain, henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, with an algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ its fraction field; `hAq` asks $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ and `hξA` that $\xi$ lie in the image of $A$; $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j\in K$ is nonzero and, by `hj`, its Laurent series is the coefficientwise image in $L$ of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $=T^{-1}\cdot\mathrm{jNum}$. A uniformiser $\varpi$ is fixed by `hϖ` ($\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$), and `hϖt` provides $\varpi_t\in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$. Write $C:=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and $\mathfrak X:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the scheme obtained as the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and the chart at $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   **The supersingular centre.** $y\subseteq C$ is a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) and satisfying `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $\jmath\in\Omega$ for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\jmath$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The rigidity hypothesis `hArig`** (a Drinfeld chart witness at every such point; its conclusion consists of seven clauses, summarised here). For every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, every element $\varpi_z$ of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ equal to the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase` and lying in the maximal ideal of that stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ whose image under `ιFin` is $z$ and whose prime satisfies the same supersingularity condition as in `hss`, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f\equiv X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ ([`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)) modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ at its maximal ideal onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, such that: (1) $e$ carries the germ of $a\in A$ to the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (2) every $L$-automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ — that is, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), which demands that for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g$ of nonzero expansion, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the ratio of those expansions, and every embedding $L\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k$ `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` — preserves $C$; (3) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, then such a $\tau$ satisfies $\tau a-a\in y'$ for all $a\in C$; (4) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially on $C/y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e$ and the map induced by $\tau$ on germs, $\theta$ fixing the constants, $\theta(X_{j})\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of $(X_0,X_1)$, $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, $c\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity; (5) two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, neither containing both $X_0$ and $X_1$, both containing $\sigma\varpi$, and containing elements $a_iX_0+b_iX_1$ plus terms of order $\ge2$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $e$ composed with the completion map; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (5) with tangent direction $X_0$, an element $a\in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the $j$-series with all exponents multiplied by $q\ell$) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the difference in $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is nondegenerate in the stated sense (for $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, the value of that form at $(a,b)$ is a unit), such that $e$ sends the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   **The chosen witness.** A point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$, an element $\varpi_z$ as above (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` image $z$ (`hy'`) satisfying the supersingularity condition (`hss'`) and with $y'=y$ (`hy'y`) are fixed, together with a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$ (`hσ₁`), power series $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units (`hu₁`, `hv₁`) and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (`hf₁`), and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$. The hypothesis `hW₁` requires for this witness exactly the seven clauses listed above, with $W_1,\sigma_1,e_1$ in place of $W,\sigma,e$.
--
--   Writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the completion map $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}\to\widehat{\mathcal O}_{\mathfrak X,z}$, $\mathrm{mkS}$ for the quotient map $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]\to S$, and $\mathrm{germY}$ for the canonical map $C\to\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ obtained from the open immersion `ιFin` and the germ at $z$, put $\Psi:=e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}:C\to S$ and $\mathfrak N:=\bigl(\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\mathrm{mkS}(X_1)\bigr)\subseteq S$.
--
--   **The remaining data.** $J$ is an ideal of $C$ which by `hJ` is the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $(\tau|_C)^{-1}\bigl(\Psi^{-1}\mathfrak N\bigr)$, taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ of $K/L$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ as above which preserve $C$. $B$ is an $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which by `hB` is the $A$-algebra underlying the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$. $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`). Further: `hR1` (two clauses) states $C\le B$ and that every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; `hR2` (three clauses) states that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that for $b\in C$ one has $b\in y$ iff $b\in\mathfrak m_W$, and that $f\in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to\operatorname{ResidueField}A$ and equivariant for the level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W$, via [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) at some unit $c$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in the kernel `hSubgroup q` of $(\bar\gamma,c)\mapsto\det\bar\gamma\cdot c^{q+1}$ and with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is reached from $\mathfrak m_W$ by some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ all of whose such translates lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; and that a level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every natural number $n$, the contraction along $\Psi$ of the $n$-th power of $\mathfrak N$ coincides with the $n$-th power of the contraction of $\mathfrak N$:
--   $$\Psi^{-1}\bigl(\mathfrak N^{\,n}\bigr)\;=\;\bigl(\Psi^{-1}\mathfrak N\bigr)^{n}$$
--   as ideals of $C$.
--
--   The statement says that the ideal of $C$ contracted from the centre $(\sigma_1\varpi_t,X_0,X_1)$ of the Drinfeld chart at a supersingular point commutes with the formation of powers, the contraction being taken along the map from the chart algebra to the completed local ring identified with a Drinfeld-type power series quotient. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_weightedCentre_pow_of_eq_pow_mul_mem_blowupChart_of_drinfeldChartWitness_linked) in the analysis of the blow-up algebra $B$ along the weighted centre $J$.
